      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <head>DOUGLAS to BARROW—at 8-30 a.m.</head>
        <p>DOUGLAS to BARROW—at 8-30 a.m.</p>
        <p>Train in convection with steamer leaves Warrington via Preston at 10-55 a.m. Special Cheap return fares from Warringtou</p>
        <p>-- - First class and Saloon 23s 64 ) Trains run Third class and Saloon 15s Od `c alongside Third class and Fore Cabin.lls Od steamers.</p>
        <p>SPECIAL NOTICE.—CIRCULAR TOUR Tickets available for g ing via Darras' and returning vice Liverpool or Fleet- wood, or vice verse, cmn now be obtained at following Fares :-- _ . - -</p>
        <p>First-class and Saloon 19s Od Third-class and Saloon 13s 6d Third-class and Fore Cabin</p>
        <p>The journey may be broken at Grange, Ulverstone (for the Lakes), Furness Abbey, or Barrow. IMPORTANT 1510TICE. --The magnificent new express steamer "DUCHESS OF DEVONSHIRE" is now on the service. There will be EXTRA sailings every SATURDAY. July Bth to SEPTEM- BER 2nd., in connection with train leaving Warrington at 2,25 p,m.—JAMES LITTLE it CO., Barrow.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>No. 1064.</p>
        <p>THROUGH LAKE-LAND TO THil ISLE OF MAN. Express Service Daily (Sundays excepted) ' BARROW to DOUGLAS—at 2-15 p.m.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>ONE PENNY</head>
        <p>ONE PENNY</p>
        <p>BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. MI WARRINGTON CORPORATION ACT, 1899. TUBERCULOSIS.</p>
        <p>IVOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that by Part IX. .1.1 of the above Act it is provided that :</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>PENALTY FOR SELLING lIILK OF DISEASED COWS.</head>
        <p>PENALTY FOR SELLING lIILK OF DISEASED COWS.</p>
        <p>Sec 96 Hyery person who knowingly sells or suffers to be sold or used for human Consumption within the borough the milk of any cow which is suffering from tuberculosis of the udder shill be liable to a penalty not exceeding ten pounds.</p>
        <p>PENALTY ON FAILING TO ISOLATE DISEASED COWS. Sec 97- Any person the milk of the cows in whose dairy is sold or suffered to be sold or used for human consumption with iu the borough wh after becoming aware that any cow in his dairy is suffering from tuberculosis of the udder keeps or per- mits to be kept such cow in any field shed or other premises along with other cows in milk shall be liable to a penalty not exceeding five pounds.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0006" n="art0006">
        <head>OBLIGATION TO NOTIFY CASES OF TUBERCULOSIS.</head>
        <p>OBLIGATION TO NOTIFY CASES OF TUBERCULOSIS.</p>
        <p>Sec. 98. Hyery dairyman who supplies milk within the borough and has in his dairy any cow affected with or suspec- ted 01 or exhibiting signs of tuberculosis of the udder shall forthwith give written notice of the fact to the Medical Officer at Health stating his narisP and address and the tuation of the dairy or premises where the cow is. Any dairyman failing to give such notice as required by this section shall be liable to a penalty not exceeding forty</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0007" n="art0007">
        <head>POWER TO TAKE BiMPLES OF MILK.</head>
        <p>POWER TO TAKE BiMPLES OF MILK.</p>
        <p>See. 99. (1.) It shall be lawful for the Medical Officer of Health or any personprovided with and if required exhibiting the authority in writing of such MedicAl Officer of Health to take within the borough for examination samples of milk pro- duced or sold or intended for sale within the borough.</p>
        <p>(2) The like powers in all respects may be exercised outside the borough by the Medical Officer of Health or such authorised person if he shall first have obtained from a Justica havint jurisdiction in the place where the sample is to be taken an urder authorising the taking of samples of the milk which order any such justice is hereby empowered to make.</p>
        <p>POWER TO INSPECT COWS AND TO TAKE SAMPLES OF MILE Sec. 100. If milk from a dairy situate within the borough is being sold or suffered to be sold or used within the borough the Medical Officer of Health or any person provided with and if requ'ring exhibiting the authority in writing of the medical officer may if accompanied by a prof erly qualified veterinary surgeon at all reasonable hours enter the dairy and inspect the cows kept therein and if the medical officer or such person has reason to suspect that any cow in the dairy is suffering from tuberculosis of the udder he may require the cow to be milked in his presence and may take samples of the milk and the milk from any particular teat shall if he so requires be kept separate and separate samples thereof be furnished. (2) If the Medical Officer of Health is of opinion that tuber- culosis is caused or is likely to be caused to persons residing in the borough from consumption of the milk supplied from a dairy situate within the borough or from any cow kept therein he shall report thereon to the Corporation and his report shall be accompanied by any report furnished to him by the veterinary surgeon and the Corporation may there- upon serve on the dairyman notice to appear before them within such time not less than twenty-four hours as may be specified in the notice to show cause why an order should not be made requiring him not to supply any milk from such dairy within the borough until the order has been withdrawn by the Corporation. (3) If the Meaiesl Officer of Health has reason to believe that milk from any dairy situate outside the borough from which milk is being sold or suffered to be sold or used within the borough is likely toca ise tuberculosis in persons residing within the borough the powers conferred by this section m.y In all respects be exercise tin the case of such dairy Provided that the Medical Officer of Health or other authorised person shall first have obtained from a Justice haying jurisdiction in the place where the dairy is situate an order authorising such entry and inspection which order any such Justice Is hereby empowered to make. (4) Every dairyman and the persons in his employment shall render such reasonable assistance to the Medical Offieer of Health or suce authorised person or veterinary surgeon es aforesaid as may be required by such medical officer person or veterinary surgeon for all or any of the purposes of this section and any person refusing such assistance or obstructing such medical officer person or veterinary P u rgeon in carrying out the purposes of this section shall be liable to a penalty no exceeding five pounds. (5) If in their opinion the dalryman fails to show cause why such an order may not be made as aforesaid the Corpora- tion may make the said order and shall forthwith serve notice of the facts on the County Council of any administrative eounty ii which the dairy is situate and on the Local Govern- ment Board and if the dairy is situate outside the borough on the Council el the borough or County District in which it is sitnete. (6) The said order shall be forthwith withdrawn on the Cor- poration or their Medical Officer of Health being satisfied that the milk supply Las been ceanged or that it is not likely to ceive tuberculosis to persons residing in the borough. (7) If any person after any such order has been made sup- plies any milk within the borough in contravention of the order or sells it for consumotioultherein he shell be liable to a penalty not excee -ling five pounds and if the offence con- tinues to a further penalty not exceeding forty shillings for every .lay during which the offence continues. (8) A dairyman shall not be liable to an action for breach cf contract if the breach be due to an order under this section.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <head>NOTICE OF PRAVISIONS OF ACT.</head>
        <p>NOTICE OF PRAVISIONS OF ACT.</p>
        <p>_ Sec. 101. The Corporation shall cause to be given public notice of the effect of the provisions of this part of this Ac', by advertisement in local newspapers and by handbills and otherwise in such manner as they think sufficient anitthis part of this Act shall come into operation at such time not being less than oae month after the first publication of such an advertisement as aforesaid as the Corporation may fix.</p>
        <p>PROCEDURE.</p>
        <p>- Sec, 102 Offences under this part of this Act mar be prose- cuted and penalties may be recovered by the Corporation be- fore a Petty Se,sional Court having jurisdiction in the place where the iairy is situate or where the otfence is committed and not otherwise.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>AS TO EXPENSES.</head>
        <p>AS TO EXPENSES.</p>
        <p>See. 103. All expenses incurrept by the Corporation in carry ing into execution the provisions Of this part of this Act shall be chargeable upon the improvement fund and improvement rate and the CorporatiOn may also charge upon the same rate any expenses incurred by them in the application by a veterinary surgeon of th, tuberculin cr other reasonable test for the purpose of discovering tuberculosis to any c•)cv whose milk is or was recently being supplied within the borough. Provided that no such test shall be applied except with the previous consent of the owner of such cow.</p>
        <p>ExECunnN or TRIS PART OF ACT BY COMMITTEE.</p>
        <p>Sec. 104. This part of tins Act may L. 2 carried into execu- tion by a committee of the Council. formed in accordance with and sulij c to the provisions of the Fourth Schedule of the Disease, el' anim,ts Act 1894 except that the committee shall consi,t wholly of the members of the Council. AND NOTICE IS fIERE,BY (+WEN that PART IX. of the above Act shall COXE INTO OPERATION on the 9th day of OCTOBER, 1899. Datcd the let day of September, 1899. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk.</p>
        <p>IF‘IDZUY, SEPTEMBER 1, 1899.</p>
