        <p>NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to a prize in this competition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of DrauwhtB equal to the value of ss, instead of cash prize, by notifying the Draughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we may state that we offer a monthly prize of 5s to the competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head o: the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winner's score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next month's competition. The win- ner may re-enter the competition if he chooses, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as follows : Two for the correct solu- tion of a problem, two for showing a dual solution, two for correcting the author's terms, and one for each minor correction. Intending competitors may commence at any time.</p>
        <p>Several of our Solvers havina succeeded in find- ing a dual solution to Problem No. 46, we have accordingly awarded those solvers 2 extra punts according to rules. The dual solution is as follows: 23-19 4-11 19-15 16-20 6 1 20-27 17-13 16-19 10— 6 20— 24 11— 8 1-10 24-27 19-24 1— 6 2-18 13-24 12-16 27-32. W. Wins 10— 6 11-16 15-10 24-23</p>
