        <p>WATER POLO. At the monthly meeting of the Liverpool and Distri Water Polo Associotion held on Monday evening S Liverpool, the question of the unfinished ma'ch,betweg' Everton and Warrington, which was contested at Vise rington on the 15th August, was referred to. After (ea; siderable discussion a motion was moved that the Maur be left in the hands of the N.C. A.S. A., and an anien ment was proposed that the match be awarded to Moir-. _, ton, but was lost by seven votes tel (i six and the ori', m•ztion was carried. The matter mill be settled by Dr, N.C.A.S.A. at their meeting at Warrington,on SaturdaP September 16th.</p>
